@startuml GuestNavigatesToSubject
' --- DIAGRAM METADATA ---
title "Sequence Diagram: Guest Navigates to a Subject Page"

' --- PARTICIPANTS ---
actor Guest
participant "Frontend (Next.js)" as Frontend
participant "Backend (FastAPI)" as Backend

' --- INITIAL STATE ---
ref over Guest, Frontend, Backend : Guest is on the Home Page

' --- FLOW OF EVENTS ---
Guest -> Frontend: Clicks on a subject card (e.g., "Computer Architecture")
activate Frontend

Frontend -> Frontend: Navigates to route '/subjects/{subjectId}'
note right of Frontend: Next.js Router handles the client-side navigation.

Frontend -> Backend: GET /api/subjects/{subjectId}
activate Backend

Backend -> Backend: Calls crud.get_subject_details(id=subjectId)
note right of Backend: Fetches subject details and eagerly loads its associated content (chapters, exams, etc.) that have status = 'approved'.

Backend --> Frontend: 200 OK [Subject with approved content]
deactivate Backend

Frontend --> Guest: Renders the Subject Detail page with all its public content.
deactivate Frontend

@enduml